[2023-12-11 13:27:08.685] -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2023-12-11 13:27:08.685]                                   NOTE
[2023-12-11 13:27:08.685] 
[2023-12-11 13:27:08.685]  There have been some changes starting with 3.2 regarding where and how libnl
[2023-12-11 13:27:08.685]  is being installed on the system in order to allow multiple libnl versions
[2023-12-11 13:27:08.685]  to be installed in parallel:
[2023-12-11 13:27:08.685] 
[2023-12-11 13:27:08.685]     - Headers will be installed in ${prefix}/include/libnl3, therefore
[2023-12-11 13:27:08.685]       you will need to add "-I/usr/include/libnl3" to CFLAGS
[2023-12-11 13:27:08.685] 
[2023-12-11 13:27:08.685]     - The library basename was renamed to libnl-3, i.e. the SO names become
[2023-12-11 13:27:08.685]       libnl-3.so., libnl-route-3.so, etc.
[2023-12-11 13:27:08.685] 
[2023-12-11 13:27:08.685]     - libtool versioning was assumed, to ease detection of compatible library
[2023-12-11 13:27:08.685]       versions.
[2023-12-11 13:27:08.685] 
[2023-12-11 13:27:08.685]  If you are using pkg-config for detecting and linking against the library 
[2023-12-11 13:27:08.685]  things will continue magically as if nothing every happened. If you are 
[2023-12-11 13:27:08.685]  linking manually you need to adapt your Makefiles or switch to using 
[2023-12-11 13:27:08.685]  pkg-config files.
[2023-12-11 13:27:08.685] 
